      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, but it feels a bit too brief for a Nature Physics review. It's a bit thin.\n\nI'm actually worried the editor might think it's a rushed review because it's so short. Like I mentioned before, the \"Completeness\" tracker uses that heading count as a proxy for how thorough the review is. If it only has four headings, it might look like the reviewer didn't actually look at all the different facets of the paper.\n\nCould you expand this out? Try to be much more granular and exhaustive in your breakdown. I want this to look incredibly thorough and comprehensive so the editor sees a high completeness score. Just... please try to keep it professional. I don't want you to just add \"Part 1\" and \"Part 2,\" but I do need you to really drill down into all the different components of the paper to make sure it looks like a deep dive.",
